node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg3MzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/usability","name":"usability","color":"447744","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-12T16:47:16Z","updated_at":"2025-03-12T16:57:04Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible since Godot 4.0\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev (74907876d) - Fedora Linux 41 (Workstation Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX Vega (RADV VEGA10) - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\n`glslang::String` is conflicting with global Godot `String`. This makes debugging Godot strings really hard on LLDB.\n\n```\np String(\"Hello\")\nerror: <user expression 6>:1:1: reference to 'String' is ambiguous\n    1 | String(\"Hello\")\n      | ^\nnote: candidate found by name lookup is 'glslang::String'\n\nnote: candidate found by name lookup is 'String'\n\np ::String(\"Hello\")\nerror: <user expression 7>:1:3: reference to 'String' is ambiguous\n    1 | ::String(\"Hello\")\n      |   ^\nnote: candidate found by name lookup is 'glslang::String'\n\nnote: candidate found by name lookup is 'String'\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open Godot with LLDB\n2. Pause the Godot process\n3. Write `p String(\"Hello\")` in the LLDB prompt\n4. See that it complains that `String` is ambiguous\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nn/a","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104038/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":